      "writtenOn": "2025-01-29T22:36:26Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I got the point of checking this to prevent unexpected behavior.\n\nBut that would change the logic flow here, the current is clearly based on status code. If you really worried about this part, it would be better to log a warning and exit earlier instead of mixing those 2 checks, while IMO it\u0027s not that necessary to have this. \nWith your new logic flow, if status is success but broadcast id is invalid, we\u0027re still proceed with using this invalid id and potentially lead to new issues, so that doesn\u0027t bring much benefits.\n\n            if (status \u003d\u003d ERROR_CODE_SUCCESS) {\n                if (broadcastId !\u003d BassConstants.INVALID_BROADCAST_ID) {\n                    // do something.\n                }\n            } else {\n                // failure case\n            }",
